---
servings: 2
source: https://sophiewyburd.substack.com/p/broccoli-and-anchovy-pasta
image: https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hQSC!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe207d1ba-31f4-432a-a91d-e800e1f6cd7b_4032x3024.jpeg
---

Add @salt{} and bring a #large pot{} of water to a boil. Break your @broccoli{1%head} down into small florets and stalk chunks that are equal in size.

Pop your @broccoli{} into the boiling water and cook it for ~{4%minutes}. Lift it straight out of the pot with a slotted spoon, and get it in a bowl of iced water. This will keep it green, and stop it from cooking.

Peel and finely slice @shallot{1} and @garlic{2%clove}.

Pour the oil from your anchovy tin and @olive oil{} into a #saute pan{}. Heat the pan over a medium heat, then add your @shallot{}, and fry them for ~{5%minutes} until they have softened.

Tip in your @garlic{}, @anchovy{50%g} and @chilli flakes{1/2%tsp}, then cook for ~{2%minutes}, squishing down the @anchovy{} into a paste as you go. 

Bring your broccoli water pan back up to a boil, then tip in your @pasta{250%g}. Cook it until it is al dente.

Drain your @broccoli{} from its iced water. Tip the @broccoli{} into the pan, along with a good splash of water. Cook this down over a low heat for ~{5%minutes}, squishing up the @broccoli{} with your wooden spoon to break it down.

When your @pasta{} is done, lift this into the pan with your slotted spoon. Add some pasta water, your @hard cheese{40%g}  and your @lemon{1} zest, then give it a good mix. Adjust the seasoning to taste.

Spoon your pasta into bowls, then top it with @lemon{} juice, more pecorino and a little more chilli, if you’d like.
